 R←Test_Misc_006(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;buff
⍝ Runs two small utilities that were quietly wrong:
⍝ * <U.AddSlash> turned an EMPTY path into "/", because ¯1↑'' yields a blank, so the test for a
⍝   trailing separator was true. An empty path must stay empty.
⍝ * <U.GetGitAttributes> offered "*.html/" and "*.iss/". A trailing slash restricts a pattern to
⍝   DIRECTORIES, so those two never matched the files they are meant to keep out of GitHub's
⍝   language statistics.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 →T.PassesIf''≡G.U.AddSlash''
 →T.PassesIf'foo/'≡G.U.AddSlash'foo'
 →T.PassesIf'foo/'≡G.U.AddSlash'foo/'
 →T.PassesIf'foo\'≡G.U.AddSlash'foo\'

 buff←G.U.GetGitAttributes
 →T.PassesIf∨/(⊂'*.html linguist-vendored=true')≡¨buff
 →T.PassesIf∨/(⊂'*.iss linguist-vendored=true')≡¨buff
 →T.PassesIf~∨/'*.html/'⍷∊buff           ⍝ A file pattern must not end in a slash ...
 →T.PassesIf~∨/'*.iss/'⍷∊buff            ⍝ ... though directory entries such as "Dist/" do

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
